### contraction inside single quotes
echo 'we'd better hurry
>>> SC1011 1:9
>>> SC2026 1:10

### short quoted word followed by a letter
printf '%s\n' 'it'd
>>> SC1011 1:18
>>> SC2026 1:19

### empty quotes followed by a letter
echo ''s
>>> SC2026 1:8

### quoted text ending in a digit followed by a letter
echo 'v1'x
>>> SC2026 1:10

### character after the closing quote is not a letter
echo 'ab'_ 'cd'9
>>> SC2026 1:16

### multi-line string ending in a contraction takes priority over the unclosed-quote warning
echo 'first line
second'd
>>> SC1011 2:7
>>> SC2026 2:8
